{
  "checked_at": "2026-10-14",
  "subject": "Local job boards for the generic markets with the most postings",
  "method": "scripts/check_robots.py's reading against each candidate's search URL with its query, then one GET of that URL to see a listing is served there -- job titles or per-job links in the page as served, not after a browser renders it. One request per host for robots and one for the page, 1.5 s apart. Read-only throughout. A page whose jobs appear only after scripts run was not added: nothing could be observed in it.",
  "markets_chosen_by": "postings per generic market across the 64 structured boards, 2026-10-13: in 477, ca 461, fr 248, sg 169, jp 143, es 132, au 129, pl 99, br 94, it 90",
  "outcome": "26 sources for 10 generic markets: fr, in, ca, au, jp 3 each; pl 4; es, br, it 2; sg 1. Each gives its market a browser channel and Web Search source hints, which generic markets had none of. Japan's three are English-language boards: the Japanese ones checked (Green, doda) refuse the search path or answer nothing readable.",
